Solaris adaptation: keep confined '..' resolution anchored at the starting FD.

The imported gnulib openat2 fallback walks components with O_NOFOLLOW, but
uses openat(current_fd, "..") at depth greater than one. A directory rename
can change that parent after descent. Solaris lacks native openat2, so do
not rely on the recorded depth alone to confine this lookup. Remember the
resolved component names, and restart at the original directory FD after
removing a component. Re-resolve with the same no-follow walk and symlink
budget. Do not retain one FD per ancestor: upstream's scarce-FD extraction
coverage and legitimate deep paths must keep working.

This is a userspace resolution strategy, not an atomic filesystem snapshot.
As with descriptor-relative extraction on Linux, callers must protect the
extraction directory against untrusted writers moving already-opened
directories. No path-based check followed by a symlink-following operation
is substituted for the descriptor walk.

Upstream fallback and documented portability limitation:
https://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/gnulib.git/commit/?id=0b97ffdf32bdab909d02449043447237273df75e
https://www.gnu.org/software/gnulib/manual/html_node/openat2.html

